<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48120" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thĕmistŏcles</span></b> , i and
		is, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θεμιστοκλῆς,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a celebrated
				Athenian commander</i>, <i>whose life is written
				by Nepos;</i> cf. <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 74, 300</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2,
				86, 351</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 16, 59</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Rep. 1,
				3, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 7, 11, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc.
				4, 19, 44</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fin. 3, 32, 104</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Them. 1,
				1</span></i> sqq.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thĕmistŏclēus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Themistocles</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consilium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 10, 8, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exsilium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10, 8, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
